## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
Implemented the full CLI Homework Auditor feature per
specs/feature-hwq-cli-homework-auditor.md and IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.
The feature was entirely absent from the codebase.

### Decisions Made
- LLMClient Protocol (structural typing) in question_generator.py instead
  of importing GitHubModelsClient directly — avoids circular imports and
  lets FakeClient satisfy the type without subclassing.
- bare requests.get for attachment downloads (no Authorization header) —
  Canvas pre-signed S3 URLs reject a second auth mechanism with HTTP 400.
- /inference suffix in GitHub Models base_url is required — the OpenAI SDK
  appends /chat/completions; omitting /inference causes every request to 404.
- per_page passed as str '50' (not int) to satisfy requests params typing
  under mypy strict mode with types-requests stubs.
- types-requests added to .pre-commit-config.yaml mypy additional_dependencies
  so the pre-commit mypy hook has the same stubs as the local environment.

### Trade-offs
- 6000-word truncation is conservative (GitHub Models free tier cap is ~8K
  tokens); accepted to give the system prompt room within the budget.
- FakeClient in tests does not subclass GitHubModelsClient to keep tests
  isolated from the real OpenAI dep — Protocol covers this cleanly.
